# Repository Structure Prompt

Design and maintain an **enterprise-grade repository structure** for **boutique-gke-sre**.

## Project Context

| Dimension | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| GCP | Single project `boutique-gke`, one private regional GKE cluster |
| Deploy | GitOps (Argo CD), Terraform IaC, GitHub Actions + WIF |
| Focus | SRE: observability, runbooks, game days, teardown |
| Domain | `biroltilki.art` → `boutique.biroltilki.art`, `argocd.boutique.biroltilki.art` |
| Environment | Single env (`boutique/`) with room to extend |

## Requirements

- Logical hierarchy, scalable, reusable, **documentation-first**
- Separate **infrastructure** (Terraform) from **applications** (GitOps) from **platform policies**
- Support single environment with extension path (e.g. `environments/stage/` later)
- Include CI/CD, GitOps, security, scripts, SRE docs, examples, diagrams, onboarding
- **Every directory** gets `README.md` — purpose, inputs, outputs, dependencies, usage
- **Every Terraform module** documents: purpose, inputs, outputs, dependencies, usage

## Layer Classification

| Layer | Directories | What belongs |
|-------|-------------|--------------|
| **Infrastructure** | `terraform/` | VPC, GKE, DNS, IAM, WIF, Cloud Armor, monitoring GCP resources |
| **Platform** | `gitops/bootstrap/`, `gitops/policies/`, `observability/` | Argo CD, Kyverno, ESO, NetworkPolicy, OTel, Prometheus, Grafana |
| **Applications** | `gitops/apps/` | Online Boutique Helm chart, Argo Applications, per-service values |
| **SRE operations** | `docs/sre/`, `scripts/game-days/`, `observability/monitoring/` | Runbooks, SLOs, alerts, game days, on-call |
| **Cross-cutting** | `.github/`, `tests/`, `scripts/bootstrap|teardown/`, root docs | CI/CD, validation, lifecycle automation, onboarding |

