## 2. Top-Level Directory Explanations

| Directory | Purpose | Does NOT contain |
|-----------|---------|------------------|
| **`.github/`** | CI/CD workflows, PR/issue templates, CODEOWNERS for review routing | Application manifests, Terraform state, secrets |
| **`terraform/`** | GCP infrastructure as code — cluster, network, DNS, IAM, edge, monitoring GCP resources | Kubernetes app manifests, Helm charts |
| **`gitops/`** | Kubernetes desired state for Argo CD — bootstrap, apps, policies | VPC/GKE provisioning (that's Terraform) |
| **`observability/`** | In-cluster and GCP monitoring config — OTel, Prometheus, Grafana, SLO/alert definitions | Runbook prose (that's `docs/sre/`) |
| **`docs/`** | All human-facing documentation — architecture, setup, SRE, operations | Executable infra (no Terraform `.tf` here) |
| **`scripts/`** | Operational helpers — game-day injection, teardown validation, prereq checks | Setup install scripts replacing `docs/setup/` |
| **`examples/`** | Minimal reference configs for copy-paste learning | Production deploy paths |
| **`tests/`** | Automated validation — Kyverno policy tests, manifest schema, Terraform tests | Live cluster integration tests (optional later) |
| **`assets/`** | Static assets — diagram sources (`.mmd`), exported images | Generated binaries, secrets |

